### DOC-001: Documents OS: uploading a valid PDF silently fails (stale alerts; file not in document count after reload)

**Retest status (23 Oct 22:20 IST): STILL OPEN** — High | Documents OS PDF upload fails | Two valid PDFs (193 B and 13.8 KB) fail. There is now an error toast, "Something went wrong on our end. Please try again shortly.", but no file is stored and the count stays at 19.

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Severity | **High** |
| Priority | P1 |
| Status | Open — Round 1 only, not re-tested |
| Evidence label | VERIFIED (R1 only); R2 UNTESTED |
| URL | https://www.streamlineos.in/knowledge (Documents OS upload) |
| Role | Owner (adityachalla01) |
| Browser | Chrome on Linux, 1280x800 viewport (automation-driven browser; member session in a separate Chrome profile) |
| Rounds | R1: observed 1/1. R2: NOT RETESTED (not attempted). |
| Repro rate | R1 1/1; R2 — |

**Preconditions:** Owner; Documents OS enabled.

**Steps to reproduce:**
1. Open Documents OS.
2. Upload `QA Test upload.pdf` (193-byte valid PDF).
3. Observe alerts; reload; check document count/list.

**Expected:** Upload succeeds with progress and success toast; file listed and counted; or a clear error.

**Actual:** No success; stale alerts shown; file not in document count after reload. No clear error.

**Evidence (textual — no screenshot files):** R1 notes (D12). R2 cleanup notes: "Failed uploads: none stored" — confirms nothing was saved.

**Impact:** Users cannot add PDFs to the knowledge base and aren't told why; Ask Documents can't use them.

**Acceptance criterion:** Valid PDF ≤10 MB uploads 5/5 with success toast and appears in list/count; failures show a specific message.

**Safe retest:** Upload `QA Test upload.pdf` once; trash it after.

