### DOC-004: Conflict banner "Load theirs" does nothing (banner stays, local text kept)

**Retest status (23 Oct 22:20 IST): STILL OPEN** — Medium | Conflict banner "Load theirs" does nothing | The banner stays, the local text is kept, nothing from the other tab loads, and there's no toast.

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Severity | **Medium** |
| Priority | P2 |
| Status | Open — run once |
| Evidence label | VERIFIED (1/1, run once) |
| URL | https://www.streamlineos.in/knowledge/wiki/doc/34 |
| Role | Owner (adityachalla01) |
| Browser | Chrome on Linux, 1280x800 viewport (automation-driven browser; member session in a separate Chrome profile) |
| Rounds | R1: not tested. R2: 1/1. (Conflict detection itself good.) |
| Repro rate | R1 —; R2 1/1 |

**Preconditions:** Same doc open in two tabs.

**Steps to reproduce:**
1. Tab 2: edit, let autosave.
2. Tab 1: type; banner appears.
3. Click "Load theirs".

**Expected:** Tab 1 loads tab 2's version and banner clears.

**Actual:** Banner ("adityachalla01 saved a newer version of this file just now. Autosave is paused — nothing you typed has been lost or overwritten") stays; TAB1 text remains. Console: 409 on /kb/pages/34.

**Evidence (textual — no screenshot files):** R2 notes; console 409.

**Impact:** Users stuck with autosave paused; can't resolve conflict except via other options/reload.

**Acceptance criterion:** "Load theirs" replaces content with server version and clears banner; autosave resumes.

**Safe retest:** Two-tab edit on a QA doc; trash after.

